{"id":"56a77f22c960a56e","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema.md","title":"ZFC Set10 Separation Subset Schema","display":"df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema — ZFC Set10 Separation Subset Schema","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema","aliases":["58-df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema"],"display":"df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema — ZFC Set10 Separation Subset Schema","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[58-ax-sep]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema — ZFC Set10 Separation Subset Schema"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d34cdb12ee59812c\" href=\"?note=d34cdb12ee59812c\" title=\"58-ax-sep\">58-ax-sep</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in V\">\\(A\\in V\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B\\subseteq A\">\\(B\\subseteq A\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi(v_0,v_1,\\ldots,v_n)\">\\(\\varphi(v_0,v_1,\\ldots,v_n)\\)</span> is a metalinguistic membership-language formula whose free variable symbols are contained in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{v_0,\\ldots,v_n\\}\">\\(\\{v_0,\\ldots,v_n\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_0\">\\(v_0\\)</span> is the separated element variable and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar p\\in V^n\">\\(\\bar p\\in V^n\\)</span> is the tuple of set values substituted for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_1,\\ldots,v_n\">\\(v_1,\\ldots,v_n\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcSet10SeparationSubsetSchema}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcSet10SeparationSubsetSchema}_S\\)</span> (schema indexed by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\">\\(\\varphi\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}set10\\text{-}separation\\text{-}subset\\text{-}schema}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ZfcSet10SeparationSubsetSchema}_S[\\varphi,n](B,A,\\bar p)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\bar p\\in V^n\\land\nB=\\{x\\in A:\\varphi(x,\\bar p(0),\\ldots,\\bar p(n-1))\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}set10\\text{-}separation\\text{-}subset\\text{-}schema}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ZfcSet10SeparationSubsetSchema}_S[\\varphi,n](B,A,\\bar p)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\bar p\\in V^n\\land\nB=\\{x\\in A:\\varphi(x,\\bar p(0),\\ldots,\\bar p(n-1))\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The brackets mark genuine metalinguistic schema indexing.  Formula-variable symbols are not conflated with the set values in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar p\">\\(\\bar p\\)</span>, and no internal truth predicate for the proper class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> is postulated.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-ax-sep","status":"resolved","id":"d34cdb12ee59812c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-sep]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"A\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"B\\subseteq A","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi(v_0,v_1,\\ldots,v_n)","display":false},{"tex":"\\{v_0,\\ldots,v_n\\}","display":false},{"tex":"v_0","display":false},{"tex":"\\bar p\\in V^n","display":false},{"tex":"v_1,\\ldots,v_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcSet10SeparationSubsetSchema}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}set10\\text{-}separation\\text{-}subset\\text{-}schema}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ZfcSet10SeparationSubsetSchema}_S[\\varphi,n](B,A,\\bar p)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\bar p\\in V^n\\land\nB=\\{x\\in A:\\varphi(x,\\bar p(0),\\ldots,\\bar p(n-1))\\}.","display":true},{"tex":"\\bar p","display":false},{"tex":"V","display":false}],"bytes":1300,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-3393","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema.md|58-df-zfc-set10-separation-subset-schema]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","d34cdb12ee59812c"]}